<menu>
    <!--
        Two entries, in two places, because they answer two different questions.

        The settings page goes under System: Settings, beside Miscellaneous, which is where this
        appliance's owner went looking for it. It cannot go INTO Miscellaneous: that page is core,
        its two hardware lists are hardcoded arrays filtered by whether /boot/kernel/NAME.ko
        exists, and it calls no plugin hook at all - so an entry there would mean editing a file
        OPNsense owns and losing the edit at every update. Nor would it belong there if it could:
        both of those lists are kldload lists, one for a crypto(9) provider and one for a thermal
        sensor module, and this driver is neither.

        No order attribute. The children of System: Settings carry none either, so they sort by
        name - Administration, General, Miscellaneous, Tunables - and "Hardware Offloading" lands
        between General and Miscellaneous on its own. A number invented here would only move it
        somewhere nobody expects.

        The status page stays under Interfaces: Diagnostics. It is a table of counters, it changes
        nothing, and it is read while something is wrong - which is a different errand from
        deciding whether offloading is on.
    -->
    <System>
        <Settings>
            <HardwareOffloading VisibleName="Hardware Offloading" cssClass="fa fa-microchip fa-fw" url="/ui/xgs/settings"/>
        </Settings>
    </System>
    <Interfaces>
        <Diagnostics>
            <XGS order="90" VisibleName="XGS Coprocessor" cssClass="fa fa-microchip fa-fw" url="/ui/xgs/status"/>
        </Diagnostics>
    </Interfaces>
</menu>
